  data:  # f2d2
    kind: work_item  # f2d2
    title: "smart-test does not select a citation test when the file it cites by string changes: bash.py:1353 rotted under a green per-PR gate and fired two crons later"  # f2d2
    status: todo_hard  # f2d2
    priority: 2  # f2d2
    parent:  # f2d2
    tags:  # f2d2
    - ci_infrastructure  # f2d2
    - smart_test  # f2d2
    isbefore: []  # f2d2
    duplicate_of: []  # f2d2
    not_duplicate_of: []  # f2d2
    pr_ref:  # f2d2
    description: "FOUND 2026-09-03 while attributing a red full-suite firing (INV-bozid).\n\nTHE MISS. `test_module_key_axis.py::test_every_cited_emission_site_still_exists`\npins that every `file:line` citation in `module_key_axis.MODULE_KEY_NOTIONS`\nstill contains its quoted anchor. The INV-sihom fix (0b8815fd2d) added lines\nto `hypergumbo_lang_mainstream/bash.py`, shifting the redirect emission from\n:1353 to :1399. The per-PR smart-test gate on that PR was GREEN: the citation\ntest lives in hypergumbo-core and names bash.py by STRING, so the import-graph\nreverse slice never selected it. It fired on the next full-suite cron\n(2026-09-03 01:00 UTC, pipeline 2189: `1 failed, 25483 passed`) and was\nrepaired in passing by 59a396395a -- two firings later, and only because a\ndifferent PR happened to touch a core file that selected it.\n\nTHE CLASS. Any test that pins a path-plus-line citation into another package\n(a \"citation test\") is invisible to a slice that follows imports. The\nsame shape exists wherever a docstring, ADR, or axis registry cites a\nproducer site by `file:line` and a test checks it against the tree.\n\nWHAT TO DO. smart-test already unions non-import selectors for data files\nand playbooks (INV-kafak's three change classes). Add a fourth: a test file\nthat contains a string literal naming a changed source path (by basename or\nrepo-relative path) is selected when that path changes. Cheap to derive from\nthe tree, and it makes a citation test fire on the commit that rots the\ncitation rather than on the next cron."  # f2d2
    fields: {}  # f2d2
- op: discuss  # 5f20
  at: '2026-09-16T06:10:32Z'  # 5f20
  by: agent  # 5f20
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5f20
  clock: 2  # 5f20
  nonce: 5f20  # 5f20
  message: "CONFIRMED LIVE 2026-09-16 on dev 81f1a69f88, with a fresh end-to-end repro of\nthis item's own example.\n\nAppended a line to\npackages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/src/hypergumbo_lang_mainstream/bash.py and\nran `smart-test --manifest`:\n\n    selected test files:                      213\n    tests/test_module_key_axis.py present:    NO\n\nThat test pins every file:line citation in module_key_axis.MODULE_KEY_NOTIONS,\nand module_key_axis.py:306 cites the string\n\"hypergumbo_lang_mainstream/bash.py\" -- so the citation and the cited file are\nboth in the tree, the citing package is selected 213 ways, and the one test that\nchecks the two against each other is not among them. Two years of import edges\ncannot see a string literal.\n\nWHY IT DID NOT GET FIXED BY THE THREE UNIONS THAT LANDED SINCE FILING. This item\nproposed \"a fourth [union]: a test file that contains a string literal naming a\nchanged source path is selected when that path changes\". Three derived unions\nnow exist in scripts/smart-test -- playbooks (:1032), catalogue YAML (:1041),\ndocs (:1054), plus fixtures (:900) and a conftest arm -- and all of them key on\nthe CHANGED path's directory. This one has to key the other way: on what the\nTEST files contain. That is why it was not swept up by the siblings, and it is\nworth stating so the next reader does not assume the family fix covered it.\n\nSECOND, UNRELATED CLAIMANT FOR THE SAME UNION. KNOWN_UNREACHABLE in\ntests/test_top_level_test_map.py says test_stdlib_version_guarded_imports.py\nneeds \"a fourth derived union in smart-test\", filed separately -- I could not\nfind that item by title search, and the tracker has no full-text search. If it\ndoes not exist, these two wants should be weighed together: both are \"a root\ntest whose subject is named by content, not by import\"."  # 5f20
